1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,737
Why Sleep Matters for Students.

2
00:00:02,687 --> 00:00:07,787
Students often sacrifice sleep to study more, but this is counterproductive.

3
00:00:07,787 --> 00:00:14,462
Sleep is when the brain consolidates memories, transferring information from short-term to long-term storage.

4
00:00:14,462 --> 00:00:19,937
A student who sleeps well after studying retains significantly more than one who stays awake.

5
00:00:19,937 --> 00:00:27,187
Sleep deprivation impairs attention, problem-solving, and emotional regulation, making learning less efficient.

6
00:00:27,187 --> 00:00:32,225
The night before an exam, sleeping well is more beneficial than staying up cramming.

7
00:00:32,225 --> 00:00:38,550
When choosing between an extra hour of study and an extra hour of sleep, sleep produces better outcomes.

